ArrayList – Definition

ArrayList Java Collection Framework ka ek class hai jo List interface ko implement karta hai.
Iska use dynamic array banane ke liye hota hai, jisme elements ko add, remove aur access easily kiya ja sakta hai.

Easy words mein

Size fixed nahi hota (automatically grow/shrink hota hai)

Index-based hota hai (0 se start)

Duplicate values allowed hoti hain

Insertion order maintain karta hai

One-line definition (exam ke liye)

ArrayList is a resizable array implementation of the List interface in Java.





LinkedList – Definition

LinkedList Java Collection Framework ka ek class hai jo List aur Deque interfaces ko implement karta hai.
Isme data nodes ke form mein store hota hai, jahan har node me data + next (aur previous) node ka reference hota hai.

Easy language mein

Data nodes mein store hota hai

Har node next (aur previous) node se linked hota hai

Insertion aur deletion fast hota hai

Duplicate elements allowed

Insertion order maintain karta hai

One-line (exam ready)

LinkedList is a collection class that stores elements as nodes connected using links.

ArrayList vs LinkedList (short difference)

ArrayList → fast access, slow insertion/deletion

LinkedList → slow access, fast insertion/deletion






List is an interface in Java that stores elements in an ordered sequence and allows duplicates.






